# What the Tauri CLI's dev watcher must NOT treat as a source change.
#
# Why this file has to exist at all: there is no `src-tauri/.gitignore`. Every
# ignore rule for this tree lives one level up in `apps/hermes-universal/.gitignore`,
# and that file deliberately UN-ignores `src-tauri/gen/android/` so our native
# customizations (MainActivity.kt, HomeBridge.kt, ScreenActivity.kt) are versioned.
# The result was that `dev:ext:desktop` watched everything Gradle and Cargo write
# while `dev:ext:android` was running, and rebuilt the desktop app over and over
# for changes that were purely Android's build output.
#
# Genuine source edits — anything under `src/`, the hand-written Kotlin, the
# manifest, `res/` — are deliberately still watched, so both surfaces pick them up.

# Cargo build trees. One per surface now (see the dev:ext:* scripts), none of it
# source.
target/
target-*/

# Regenerated by tauri-build on every single build.
gen/schemas/
gen/apple/

# The Android project is tracked, so it cannot be ignored wholesale — only what
# Gradle, Cargo and the Tauri CLI generate inside it. Kept in step with
# gen/android/.gitignore and gen/android/app/.gitignore, which declare the same
# set to git.
gen/android/build/
gen/android/.gradle/
gen/android/.tauri/
gen/android/local.properties
gen/android/tauri.settings.gradle
gen/android/app/build/
gen/android/app/.cxx/
gen/android/app/tauri.build.gradle.kts
gen/android/app/tauri.properties
gen/android/app/proguard-tauri.pro
gen/android/app/src/main/assets/tauri.conf.json
gen/android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
# wry regenerates RustWebView.kt here on every Android build (and build.rs
# rewrites it right after — see patch_android_get_cookies).
gen/android/app/src/main/**/generated/
